GIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Her 2 only   See also  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  The well defined 1 8cm nodule noted grossly appears to represent a hamartoma with secondary involvement by lobular carcinoma in situ and minute foci of invasive lobular carcinoma within it  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Dumaine  REMOVE_MRN and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm portion of tan pink fibrofatty tissue which is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink lymph node  The lymph node is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Dumaine  REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm left simple mastectomy specimen with a black stitch designating the axillary tail  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm tan pink skin ellipse with an eccentric REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm tan pink nipple which comes to 1 0cm of the supero lateral skin margin  The posterior margin is inked black  and the anterior margin is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm grey white vaguely stellate nodule in the upper outer quadrant which comes to 0 7cm of the anterior margin and greater than 4cm of the posterior margin  Located 1 5cm postero medial to the aforementioned nodule in the upper outer quadrant is a well defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm grey white to tan pink rubbery mass which comes to 2 5cm of the posterior margin  Eccentrically within this nodule are cavities consistent with previous biopsy sites  Antero inferior to this rubbery mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm indurated grey white nodule which is greater than 4cm of the posterior margin and 0 7cm from the rubbery mass  Located antero superior to the rubbery mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm grey white to tan yellow indurated nodule which is also greater than 4cm from the posterior margin and 0 8cm from the rubbery mass  Located in the mid inner breast tissue 2 0cm from the posterior margin is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm cavity containing packing material which is consistent with a previous biopsy site  Noted in the mid upper breast tissue is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm indurated area with a silver metal clip which comes to 1 7cm of the posterior margin  Noted in central breast tissue is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm region of hemorrhage which is  3 5cm from the posterior margin  Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals no apparent lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire nodule from upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire rubbery nodule from upper outer quadrant  including closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire indurated nodule antero inferior to rubbery nodule in upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire indurated nodule antero superior to the rubbery nodule in the upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire cavity from mid inner breast tissue with closest posterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule with clip to closest posterior margin from mid upper breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of tissue with clip from mid upper breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Region of hemorrhage in central breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from upper outer quadrant which may represent lymph nodes  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  LEFT AXILLA SENTIN